  "content": {
    "id": "p16-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "If $x$ is subtracted from both the numerator and denominator of $\\frac{3}{4}$, the result is $\\frac{7}{10}$. Find $x$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=\\frac{2}{3}$.\n\nForm $\\frac{3-x}{4-x}=\\frac{7}{10}$ and clear the denominator.",
      "worked": "The denominator requires $x\\ne4$. Multiply both sides by $10(4-x)$, then expand and solve.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{3-x}{4-x}&=\\frac{7}{10}\\\\10(3-x)&=7(4-x)\\\\30-10x&=28-7x\\\\30&=28+3x\\\\2&=3x\\\\x&=\\frac{2}{3}\\end{align*}$$\nCheck:\n$$\\frac{3-\\frac{2}{3}}{4-\\frac{2}{3}}=\\frac{\\frac{7}{3}}{\\frac{10}{3}}=\\frac{7}{10}.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 55
  },
